# ============================================================================
# SECRETS — never commit. These hold live credentials / private keys / state.
# ============================================================================
# the secrets tree: per-app .env + pems + license (apps/<app>/), shared/tls, infra/ (seaweedfs, etherpad,
# cluster-creds, region_secret). Ignore ALL of it — but KEEP the redacted .env.example templates + READMEs
# so the structure stays self-documenting in git (a dev sees each app's required keys without any secret).
iac/secrets/**
!iac/secrets/**/
!iac/secrets/**/.env.example
!iac/secrets/**/README.md
# cluster admin access
**/kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig-*
kubeconfig*
# terraform state (contains ALL generated secrets) + generated tfvars
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
iac/terraform/terraform.tfvars
# ansible vault (encrypted, but keep it out to be safe) + vault password file
**/vault.yml
**/vault.yaml
**/.vault_pass*
# any env file with real values (allow *.example / *.sample templates)
*.env
!*.env.example
!*.env.sample
!*.env.template
.env
# private keys / certs (belt-and-suspenders; .secrets/ already covers the real ones)
*.pem
*.key
!**/*.pub
# SSH keypair for ansible (private key has NO extension) — keep only the .pub
iac/ansible/ssh/*
!iac/ansible/ssh/*.pub
# generic SSH private-key names
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519
**/id_ecdsa
# AWS / cloud credentials
**/.aws/
**/credentials
**/*credentials*
# licence files
**/license.txt
**/licence.txt

# ============================================================================
# Build / OS noise
# ============================================================================
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.log
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
